 or not another act moved that registry.\r\nevidence: tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_reattestation_outside_the_amendment_scope_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_reattestation_inside_the_amendment_scope_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_is_read_from_trunk_not_from_the_lane; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_mixed_approval_and_reattestation_act_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_mixed_act_reattesting_outside_its_amendment_scope_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_sittings_sections_each_take_their_own_act; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_sittings_act_outside_its_kinds_tokens_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_in_two_registries_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_whose_first_approval_returned_everything_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_copying_a_registry_neither_section_moved_is_widened; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_on_a_csv_carrier_authorizes_the_copy_it_writes; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_on_a_markdown_needs_carrier_authorizes_its_copy; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_across_a_needs_carrier_conversion_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_plain_flip_across_a_needs_carrier_conversion_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_an_unauthorized_registrys_obsolete_copy_is_still_widened; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_tier_act_naming_an_unaccepted_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_first_approval_in_an_act_naming_an_unaccepted_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_an_act_omitting_its_verdict_is_still_tied_to_an_accepted_one; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_an_accepted_sitting_over_other_rows_does_not_authorize_this_act; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_single_kind_verdict_over_other_rows_does_not_authorize; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_must_judge_the_rows_it_reattests; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_single_kind_first_approval_of_its_judged_row_merges; tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_a_ledger_only_approval_outside_the_scope_is_refused; tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_a_backed_ledger_only_approval_on_an_ordinary_lane_is_admitted; tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_an_unbacked_ledger_only_approval_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_alone_in_its_registry_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_the_acted_set_names_a_retired_rows_registry; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_lone_retirement_on_a_held_rung_is_refused_by_row; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_outside_the_amendment_scope_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_no_accepted_verdict_rules_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_beside_another_act_in_its_registry_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_plain_MEANING_reattestation_is_refused_naming_the_row_and_the_mark; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_MEANING_BLESS_reattestation_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_row_tagged_two_ways_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_ruling_the_row_plain_MEANING_is_refused_naming_the_verdict; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_blessing_the_row_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_carrying_a_plain_MEANING_reattestation_is_refused_whole; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_with_a_blessed_reattestation_merges; tests/test_held_status.py::test_the_ledger_clarity_arm_is_retired; tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_a_held_retirement_is_refused\r\n\r\nTC-398\r\nmethod: The approved-text digest ignores a row id, Status, traced cells and empty-versus-absent cells, but changes for an approved cell. The amendment brief renders one judged-text digest per shown row; reservation writes those identities, accepted and failed outcome rewrites preserve them, and a held CLARITY act whose committed text differs, or whose binding lacks an identity, is refused before launch.\r\nexpected: Satisfies LLR-359: The approved-text digest is formed from a row's nonempty approved cells, excluding its id and Status, so carrier representation and an absent versus empty cell give the same identity. An amendment brief renders one judged-text identity line for each shown row. Reservation writes those identities in the binding, and rewriting the binding as accepted or failed preserves them. A held CLARITY re-attestation is actable only when the accepted binding's identity equals the committed row's approved-text digest; an absent, malformed or unequal identity yields a row-naming refusal before launch.\r\nevidence: tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_the_amendment_brief_states_each_shown_rows_digest; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_bind_pending_records_the_briefs_identities; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_record_outcome_keeps_the_identity_cell; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_whose_text_changed_after_the_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_whose_binding_has_no_identity_is_refused; tests/test_coordinator_act.py::test_the_act_turn_refuses_before_launch_when_held_text_moved; tests/test_held_status.py::test_the_digest_ignores_the_id_status_and_traced_cells; tests/test_held_status.py::test_the_digest_is_carrier_blind_and_empty_equals_absent; tests/test_held_status.py::test_the_digest_has_the_done_when_shape; tests/test_held_status.py::test_a_binding_round_trips_its_identities; tests/test_held_status.py::test_read_requested_ignores_the_identity_cell; tests/test_held_status.py::test_a_malformed_or_absent_identity_cell_reads_as_no_identity; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_bound_to_the_exact_text_is_owed\r\n\r\nLLR-246\r\ndetail: staged_status_moves(root, base, head) reports every change to a status cell of an off-spine registry between two trees or between a base and the index, rows added or removed with a status included; the needs file is read for its stakeholder tier. held_status_refusal(dial, moves) refuses each move whose registry rung the dial holds, per the rung maps in kitlib/authority.py (re-exported by agent_common as APPROVAL_RUNGS), which gain the assumptions registry at DevStg-Boundary and the needs file, needs and stakeholders alike, at DevStg-Needs; an unmapped registry reads held. Every live judgement reads the dial through kitlib.authority.dial_at, which reads the dial committed in a named tree, or staged in the index, translating each legacy spelling exactly as agent_common.approval_through does and printing nothing; no live judgement reads the working file. Every loop writer, under the loop marker, runs the refusal through agent_common.loop_held_status_refusal on the exact tree it is about to write, against the dial committed on trunk, immediately before its commit or commit-tree: the claim (integrate._claim_locked) and the mint (intake._mint) both commit through bookkeeping._commit_object, which performs the check between write-tree and commit-tree against the dial committed in the commit's parent; every handback commit, including _commit_residue_as_is; and agent_common.commit_telemetry. The refusal fires only outside a claimed lane: a handback commit inside a lane passes, and its lane is judged at landing. A check step `held-status` in the pre-commit failing set judges a squash landing by its lane commits and, armed when the loop marker is set outside a claimed lane, covers a session commit made through the hook, judging the index against the dial committed at HEAD; during a merge it judges the staged result against its first parent, less each status a merged side already carries. A person's commit, made with no loop marker, other than a squash landing, is not judged where it is made; every lane is judged at landing. A held approval claim is a live status move into approval, a born-approved row, an approval-cell or Status movement in its copy, or a copied approved row's retirement; it is a claim only when it is present against every parent. The held set is every tier of the snapshotted registries, with an unmapped registry held. A lane rider judges each lane commit after parent-first, and the merge slot and an admitted squash use that rider; a non-admitted squash judges its index as one lane commit. The dial is read at trunk HEAD for a landing and at the commit's parent for the marked arm. A held claim is refused unless it is a copy claim whose live row is unchanged and approving on both sides, equals its copy at the commit, and has an accepted CLARITY amendment verdict binding its equal approved-text digest. An unreadable or unparseable live registry or copy yields a refusal naming it. The slot's loop-lane held-status rung does not run. Under the loop marker, a commit outside a claimed lane, other than a squash landing, is refused when it moves a held status or makes a held approval claim; a marked commit inside a lane is judged at landing. An unmarked plain trunk commit is not judged. A row tagged both MEANING and CLARITY reads MEANING, and a MEANING+BLESS ruling is no exception.\r\n\r\nLLR-249\r\ndetail: kitlib/authority.py holds a pure dial comparison: dial_from_config(table) reads human_approval_through from a parsed policy table, an absent or legacy value reading as the most-held rung with no printed warning; holds_under(dial, rung) compares on the ladder. APPROVAL_RUNGS and the spine rung map move there and agent_common re-exports them. held_status.committed_status_moves(root, rev) lists status moves between rev and its first parent across the spine and off-spine registries. check_trajectory.loop_held_status_findings visits every non-merge commit reachable from trunk, lane commits included, once each; a merge commit is skipped because its changes are those of the commits it merges, each visited on its own, and a root commit is diffed against the empty tree. For each commit carrying the loop trailer it judges the moves against the dial in that commit's own policy file; each hit is one advisory naming the commit, the row and the rung.\r\n\r\nLLR-278\r\ndetail: acceptance_record.merge_approval_refusal applies the additional adjudication bounds whenever any claimed row records a scope, including a mixed lane, and calls reattest_scope_refusal for that scope-bound lane. A malformed combined token is refused by name; an act-free delta has no scope refusal. reattested_between reads the ledger at the merge base and the head and takes the ids re-attested by the entries whose seq the base does not hold, refusing by name when either side does not parse. Every such id outside amendment_scope - the union of the claimed amendment rows' own amendment scope, including their amendment:<id> tokens when a combined sitting claims them, empty when none is claimed - is refused by name before the first-approval judgement runs. Every approval act in the lane�s complete acted set - a live flip or born-approved row, a ledger-only approval, or a re-attestation - is refused when any row it approves lacks an APPROVE ruling in an accepted first-approval part or any row it re-attests lacks a CLARITY ruling, or a MEANING ruling carrying the bless mark, in an accepted amendment part among the branch's bindings, whether or not the act names a verdict; a named verdict must also authorize every row its act re-attests in the same way, and acts already on trunk are not re-read. An act that both approves rows and re-attests rows, claimed either by two single-kind rows or by one combined sitting's per-kind tokens, merges when each half lies inside its claiming row's own kind scope, whether their rows are in one registry or different ones; an id under another combined kind authorizes neither half, a snapshot is WIDENED only when the complete acted set holds no approved or re-attested row in that registry identity, a row the act ledger names being placed in the registry its id's tier names whether or not the row remains in the live registry at the head, so a retirement authorizes its own registry's copy: every carrier path of an authorized registry, including a deleted obsolete carrier copy, is authorized, while an unauthorized registry's copy is WIDENED on every carrier path.\r\ntest_refs: TC-278; TC-331\r\n\r\nLLR-359\r\ndetail: The approved-text digest is formed from a row's nonempty approved cells, excluding its id and Status, so carrier representation and an absent versus empty cell give the same identity. An amendment brief renders one judged-text identity line for each shown row. Reservation writes those identities in the binding, and rewriting the binding as accepted or failed preserves them. A held CLARITY re-attestation is actable only when the accepted binding's identity equals the committed row's approved-text digest; an absent, malformed or unequal identity yields a row-naming refusal before launch.\r\ntest_refs: TC-398; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_the_amendment_brief_states_each_shown_rows_digest; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_bind_pending_records_the_briefs_identities; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_record_outcome_keeps_the_identity_cell; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_whose_text_changed_after_the_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_coordinator_act.py::test_the_act_turn_refuses_before_launch_when_held_text_moved\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
