{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"Reconciled the checkpoint set. I changed only spine registries; no tests were edited and pytest was not run.\n\nCheckpoint amendments:\n\n- SR-208 `title`: “The loop never changes a status the approval level holds for a human” → “Held-rung changes are refused before they land”. Aligns the title with lane and marked-commit enforcement.\n\n- SR-208 `coincident`: “The need asks for a held tier changed only by a person; the loop's own status changes refused before they land is that outcome for the one writer the kit controls, and whether a person's change reflects judgement is not this row's claim.” → “The need asks for a held tier changed only by a person; refusing an unbound lane approval claim and a marked autonomous commit that moves held state before either lands preserves that outcome, and whether a person's change reflects judgement is not this row's claim.” Aligns the coincidence rationale with the implemented routes.\n\n- SR-228 `acceptance_criteria`: “…the recorded act names the verdict for later audit…” → “…when supplied, the recorded act names the verdict for later audit…”. `--verdict` is optional and is recorded when present.\n\n- LLR-246 `title`: “Refusing a loop-made status change on a held off-spine registry, at every loop writer” → “Refusing held-rung claims from a lane or marked autonomous commit”. Matches the state-based lane rule and narrowed marker arm.\n\n- LLR-278 `test_refs`: identity-pipeline test nodes → “TC-278; TC-331”. Removes tests for the separate identity decision.\n\n- TC-278 `method`, `expected`, `evidence`: removed the identity-pipeline assertions/nodes. Those belong to LLR-359/TC-398; TC-278 now covers only merge scope and approval-act admission.\n\n- TC-241 `evidence`: appended `test_a_held_CLARITY_reattestation_bound_to_the_exact_text_lands` and `test_held_text_changed_after_its_CLARITY_verdict_is_refused_at_the_slot`. Completes evidence for SR-208’s bounded lane exception.\n\n- IF-129 `requestors`: added `scripts/held_status`, `scripts/adjudicate_brief`, `scripts/adjudicate_act`. These call the digest seam.\n\n- IF-129 `data`: shortened the expanded contract to “split_changed_cells; approved_text_digest(registry, id_col, row) -> sha256:<16 lowercase hex>”. Keeps the seam pointers within the data-cell budget.\n\n- IF-196 `data`: replaced the stale `rows_at` declaration with the held-status seam’s current exported vocabulary, including `HELD_TIERS`, `HELD_PATHS`, `registry_held`, and `marked_refusal`.\n\n- IF-196 `notes`: “the degrade every reader of this module shares” → “the status-move readers’ degrade”. Limits the empty-delta statement to its actual callers.\n\n- IF-287 `requestors`: added `scripts/held_status`. It reads accepted binding identities.\n\n- IF-287 `data`: shortened to the current binding/identity reader and writer vocabulary.\n\n- IF-296 `data`: shortened to the current act derivation and held-text identity-refusal vocabulary.\n\nNo new ID was allocated; existing Drafted LLR-359 and TC-398 remain the identity pipeline’s single home.\n\nBuilder-list reconciliation:\n\n- Confirmed: IF-196 moved to `held_status`; `rows_at` remains owned by `acceptance_record` and was removed from IF-196.\n- Confirmed: IF-129, IF-287, and IF-296 consumers/data now match implemented callers and symbols.\n- Confirmed: SR-208/LLR-246 now describe lane claims and marked autonomous commits rather than the retired slot rung.\n- Confirmed: SR-228’s verdict is optional in the recorded act.\n- Extended: removed identity assertions from LLR-278/TC-278 and retained them solely in LLR-359/TC-398, because they are a separate decision with distinct implementation and tests.\n- Refuted: none.\n\nARMS MAP:\n\n| Obligation | TC clause | Existing exercise |\n|---|---|---|\n| SR-208 bounded CLARITY lane exception | TC-241 expected first sentence | `test_a_held_CLARITY_reattestation_bound_to_the_exact_text_lands`; `test_held_text_changed_after_its_CLARITY_verdict_is_refused_at_the_slot` |\n| SR-208 claim classes, held/unmapped rungs, unreadable carriers | TC-241 method/expected | `test_a_live_flip_into_approval_is_a_claim`; `test_a_copy_entry_move_or_retirement_is_a_claim`; `test_an_unmapped_registry_is_held`; unreadable-registry git case |\n| SR-208 parent walk and squash handling | TC-241 method | lane-walk and both squash git cases |\n| SR-208 marked outside-lane arm / unmarked and in-lane exclusions | TC-241 expected | hook, writer, in-lane, and unmarked-trunk git cases |\n| LLR-246 lane rider, marker arm, writer routes | TC-241 method/expected | held-status unit and real-git writer/landing cases |\n| LLR-249 history reporting | TC-243 | `tests/test_loop_provenance.py` |\n| SR-228 / LLR-278 scope, accepted rulings, retirement copies | TC-278 expected | snapshot-reader scope, ruling, ledger-only, and retirement cases |\n| LLR-359 digest, brief identity, binding preservation, pre-launch refusal | TC-398 expected | adjudicate-brief, sitting, adjudicate-act, coordinator-act, and held-status identity tests |\n\nGaps: none identified in the reconciled set.\n\nChecks:\n\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict`: `check_trajectory: clean (969 work item(s), 856 done (88%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic).` Standing advisories remain.\n- `trace.py --strict`: `orphans=0 integrity=0 … interface-findings=0`; exit 0.\n- TOML parsing, LF-only verification, and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Pytest: not run, as instructed."}}
